          "A healthy hierarchy is functional: someone coordinates, someone decides when a decision is needed, someone carries responsibility. It is not ontological: no one is worth more. Pay and titles may reflect responsibility, skill or market forces; they never measure a person’s value before God (1 Sam 16:7). Authority exists for the good of those under it (Rom 13:4; Heb 13:17), and will be judged by that standard (Luke 12:48; Jas 3:1).",
